========================================================================
C. JITTER TOLERANCE — strut length error dd vs gates
========================================================================
  Tree/seed lock (forward psi=0 exact): the whole per-link defect sits on
  the back gate, psi_b = 2*omega*dd  =>  g_b = cos^16(omega*dd).
  Entrained equilibrium (E6 P2: comma tempered evenly): psi_f = psi_b =
  omega*dd  =>  both gates cos^16(omega*dd/2). Tempering doubles tolerance.
  gate >= 0.9:
    tree lock:  |dd| <= 0.114635/omega     = 3.65% of strut length pi/omega
    tempered:   |dd| <= 0.229270/omega     = 7.30% of strut length
      omega=1.9424: tree 0.0590, tempered 0.1180
      omega=2.0944: tree 0.0547, tempered 0.1095
      omega=2.5139: tree 0.0456, tempered 0.0912
      omega=2.7002: tree 0.0425, tempered 0.0849
  gate >= 0.99:
    tree lock:  |dd| <= 0.035440/omega     = 1.13% of strut length pi/omega
    tempered:   |dd| <= 0.070881/omega     = 2.26% of strut length
      omega=1.9424: tree 0.0182, tempered 0.0365
      omega=2.0944: tree 0.0169, tempered 0.0338
      omega=2.5139: tree 0.0141, tempered 0.0282
      omega=2.7002: tree 0.0131, tempered 0.0263
  NOTE the tolerance as a FRACTION of the strut length is omega-independent:
  3.65%/7.29% (gate 0.9), 1.13%/2.26% (gate 0.99). Blue-noise foam placement
  error is ~10-20% of d  =>  raw seeded shells sit at gates ~0.5-0.7 (measured
  cube: mean 0.6) — annealing/entrainment-grown skins are REQUIRED, or picks
  must be mined for equal lengths (P3).
