========================================================================
E. RING GEOMETRY FACTOR — seeded plane alignment gpl(N)
========================================================================
  Ring seeder sets both planes transverse to the OUTGOING chord; for a
  planar ring, n1 = z for every voice and n2 = u_out x z. On link k->k+1:
  source axial factor 1 exactly; receiver picks up the polygon turn 2pi/N:
  axj = cos^2(2pi/N), (n2_i.n2_j)^2 = cos^2(2pi/N)  =>  gpl = cos^4(2pi/N).
  If kappa_align settles the axes onto the bisector: gpl -> cos^4(pi/N).
    N=  4: seeded gpl = 0.0000   bisector gpl = 0.2500
    N=  5: seeded gpl = 0.0091   bisector gpl = 0.4284
    N=  6: seeded gpl = 0.0625   bisector gpl = 0.5625
    N=  8: seeded gpl = 0.2500   bisector gpl = 0.7286
    N= 12: seeded gpl = 0.5625   bisector gpl = 0.8705
    N= 16: seeded gpl = 0.7286   bisector gpl = 0.9253
    N= 24: seeded gpl = 0.8705   bisector gpl = 0.9662
  N=6 pays a 9x conductance penalty vs N=12 at seed; N=4 is dead (turn=90deg).
